0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  B8Script interpreter for the Intel 8080
0000                             ;  Spec: docs/b8script.md (2026-11-23).
0000                             ;  Design follows the Z80 interpreter (z80/b8s-z80.asm), with 8080 opcodes
0000                             ;  only.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Three switches, set in the EQU lines below:
0000                             ;    CPM      0 = generic ROM build (KEY/CONOUT at fixed addresses)
0000                             ;             1 = CP/M 2.2 .COM file: loads the file named on the command line
0000                             ;    CHECKED  0 = no checks (spec: the programmer is responsible)
0000                             ;             1 = starts with every variable at 0 and every word undefined,
0000                             ;                 and stops on every error in the spec's table (and Ctrl-C)
0000                             ;                 with a four-line report: the letter and the place as line
0000                             ;                 and column, the text there, and both stacks. See `error`.
0000                             ;    ANSI     1 = the four console codes (`@ `^ `_ `?) send ANSI escape
0000                             ;                 sequences through CONOUT
0000                             ;             0 = they call four routines of the machine's own instead:
0000                             ;                 CONAT, CONCLS, CONEOL and CONCUR (see the equates)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  In every build Ctrl-C stops a running program (an unchecked build stops
0000                             ;  without a word): see the console layer for the rules, the held key and
0000                             ;  the break-off cell.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Assembler: asm80 (https://maly.github.io/asm80-node/), I8080 mode.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                CPM:      EQU   0   ; 1 = CP/M .COM build
0000                CHECKED:   EQU   1   ; 1 = checked build
0000                ANSI:     EQU   1   ; 1 = the console codes send ANSI sequences
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Register use, everywhere in the interpreter
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    BC   IP: the address of the next program character to read
0000                             ;    HL   TOS: the top data-stack cell is kept here, not in memory
0000                             ;    SP   the data stack: (SP) is NOS, the cell under TOS. The data stack is
0000                             ;         the 8080"s own stack, which is what the spec"s machine-code contract
0000                             ;         needs ("the data cells above the return address").
0000                             ;    A DE scratch. Every handler is entered with HL = TOS and may use A, DE.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The return stack pointer has no register (the 8080 has no spare pair): it
0000                             ;  is the RAM word RSP. Only rpop, rpushd and ")" (and the checks) touch it.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  One-byte calls. The routines used most are reached with RST, one byte
0000                             ;  instead of three. (asm80 wants the vector number: RST 1 = RST 08h.)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RST 1  08h  rpop    pop the return stack into HL
0000                             ;    RST 3  18h  drop    drop TOS, then next character     (ends a handler)
0000                             ;    RST 4  20h  neg16   HL = -HL
0000                             ;    RST 5  28h  putc    print A
0000                             ;    RST 6  30h  next    next character                    (ends a handler)
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  RST 3 and RST 6 never return: an RST is a CALL, so the first thing each
0000                             ;  of them does is POP D to throw the return address away.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The CP/M build can't own page zero, so the block from `vecs` to `vecend`
0000                             ;  (image addresses 0108h-0133h) is copied to 0008h-0033h when it starts. The
0000                             ;  code in that block has no jumps inside itself, so it works at either place.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  Dispatch. PTAB holds one byte per punctuation character: the low byte of
0000                             ;  its handler's address. The high byte is worked out from the character:
0000                             ;  the handlers of the first NPG1 characters (in code order) start in the
0000                             ;  image's second page, the rest in its first. The layout below keeps to
0000                             ;  that, and testing/chktab.py checks it in every build.
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  What the 8080 lacks, and what replaces it: no JR (JMP/Jcc), no DJNZ, no
0000                             ;  SBC HL (byte-wise SUB/SBB, or negate and DAD), no shifts on register pairs
0000                             ;  (DAD H doubles; RAL/RAR through A), no LDIR/CPIR (small loops).
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                             ;  Memory map. Everything the interpreter writes is in four RAM pages:
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;    RSPAGE   return stack, 112 entries (the pointer stays inside this page)
0000                             ;    DSPAGE   data stack, 127 cells (the top four bytes of the page are spare,
0000                             ;             so a full stack runs two bytes into the page below)
0000                             ;    LETPAGE  letter cells: A..Z at +00h..+33h, a..z at +40h..+73h (so a word
0000                             ;             cell is always 64 bytes below its variable), the heap pointer at
0000                             ;             +7Ch, interpreter variables in the gaps, and the -n? line buffer
0000                             ;             at +80h..+FFh
0000                             ;    PROG     the program text, NUL-terminated; the heap starts after the NUL
0000                             ; 
0000                             ;  The stacks sit below the letter page, so "the program's own space" (what
0000                             ;  the checked build lets ! and . write) is the single range from the letter
0000                             ;  page up to the heap limit. Each stack has a guard band: the data stack can
0000                             ;  overrun by a cell or two (and the calls made while it is full, the error
0000                             ;  report's included) into the top 32 bytes of the return-stack page, which
0000                             ;  are never used, and the return stack by one entry into the page below it.
0000                             ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0000                          IF   CPM   
                    BDOS:     EQU   0005h   
                    EXIT:     EQU   0000h   ; warm boot
                    BASE:     EQU   0100h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IFN   CPM   
0000                             ; ---- generic machine: edit these to suit -----------------------------------
0000                KEY:      EQU   0FF06h   ; a waiting key in A, or A = 0 if none is
0000                             ;   waiting. The zero flag must match A
0000                             ;   (end the routine with ORA A / RET).
0000                CONOUT:   EQU   0FF03h   ; print the character in A
0000                EXIT:     EQU   0FF09h   ; where to go when the program ends
0000                             ;   KEY and CONOUT must preserve BC, DE and HL.
0000                RSPAGE:   EQU   80h   ; 8000h return stack
0000                DSPAGE:   EQU   81h   ; 8100h data stack
0000                LETPAGE:   EQU   82h   ; 8200h letter cells and line buffer
0000                PROG:     EQU   8300h   ; where the loader puts the program text
0000                HEAPLIM:   EQU   0F0h   ; the heap must stay below F000h (a page)
0000                BASE:     EQU   0000h   ; where the image starts
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                          IF   (1-CPM)*(1-ANSI)   
                                 ; ---- generic machine with ANSI = 0: the console codes call these ------------
                    CONAT:    EQU   0FF0Ch   ; `@  cursor to row E, column L, both from 0
                                 ;     (DE and HL hold the whole cells). May
                                 ;     change A, DE and HL
                    CONCLS:   EQU   0FF0Fh   ; `^  clear the screen and home the cursor
                    CONEOL:   EQU   0FF12h   ; `_  clear from the cursor to the end of the line
                    CONCUR:   EQU   0FF15h   ; `?  cursor off if A = 0 (the zero flag is set
                                 ;     to match), on if not. May change A, DE, HL
                                 ;   All four must preserve BC; CONCLS and CONEOL also DE and HL.
0000                          ENDIF      
0000                MSLOOP:   EQU   40   ; n? inner loop count for about 1 ms (1-255;
0000                             ; the wait for a second Ctrl-C uses it too):
0000                             ; each pass calls getk once, so tune it for
0000                             ; your clock and your KEY routine
0000                             ; letter-page layout (offsets inside LETPAGE)
0000                LET:      EQU   LETPAGE*256   
0000                HEAP:     EQU   LET+7Ch   ; the heap pointer
0000                RSP:      EQU   LET+34h   ; gap after Z: the return stack pointer;
0000                BRKCNT:   EQU   LET+36h   ;   the break check's countdown;
0000                NPEND:    EQU   LET+38h   ;   minus the address of the program's end
0000                             ;   (the heap"s first byte), for the checked "_'
0000                SEED:     EQU   LET+76h   ; gap after z: the random seed, the cell whose
0000                             ;   address `. gives. Nothing sets it at the
0000                             ;   start but the checked build's clearing;
0000                KEYBUF:   EQU   LET+7Ah   ;   a key read by the break check and
0000                             ;   held for the next "?" (0: none);
0000                BRKOFF:   EQU   LET+7Bh   ;   the break-off cell: a program that stores a
0000                             ;   non-zero byte here gets Ctrl-C as a key
0000                LBHDR:    EQU   LET+7Eh   ; CP/M BDOS 10 header: max, count
0000                LINEBUF:   EQU   LET+80h   ; -n? text, ending in CR
0000                RSTOP:    EQU   RSPAGE*256+0E0h   ; empty return stack: the 32 bytes above it
0000                             ; take calls made while the data stack is full
0000                DSTOP:    EQU   DSPAGE*256+0FCh   ; empty data stack. The four bytes above it
0000                             ; are spare: a character can pop two cells
0000                             ; too many before the checked build sees it,
0000                             ; and the next call must not land on the
0000                             ; letter cells.
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                             ;  The first 49 bytes: the entry, then the RST routines, with small handlers
0000                             ;  and routines filling the gaps between them. Generic: this IS page zero.
0000                             ;  CP/M: it is the start of the .COM file, and 0108h-0133h is also copied to
0000                             ;  page zero (see the header).
0000                             ; =============================================================================
0000                          .ORG   BASE   
0000                          IF   1-(1-CPM)*CHECKED   
                              LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; 00  reset, or the start of the .COM file
0000                          ENDIF      
0000   C3 D0 05               JMP   start   ; In the checked generic build this is at 0000h
0003                             ;   (and `start` sets SP): its first byte, C3h,
0003                             ;   is what an undefined word runs into, as
0003                             ;   CP/M's own JMP at 0000h is in a .COM: e_hi.
0003                          IF   (1-CPM)*CHECKED   
0003   00 00 00               DB   0,0,0   ; 03  spare
0006                          ENDIF      
0006   CF           RDROP:    RST   1   ; 06  drop the top of the return stack, then
0007   DF                     RST   3   ;     drop TOS (a spent flag) and go on
0008                VECS:        
0008                             ; ---- RST 1: rpop: pop the return stack into HL (DE is lost) -----------------
0008   2A 34 82     RPOP:     LHLD   RSP   ; 08
000B   5E                     MOV   E,M   
000C   23                     INX   H   
000D   56                     MOV   D,M   
000E   23                     INX   H   
000F   22 34 82               SHLD   RSP   
0012   EB                     XCHG      
0013   C9                     RET      ; 13  (so RST 2 is not used)
0014   EB           H_TOR:    XCHG      ; 14  "{" TOS to the return stack; rpushd
0015   C3 B3 00               JMP   rpushd   ;     brings up the new TOS
0018                             ; ---- RST 3: drop TOS, then next ---------------------------------------------
0018   D1           RST18:    POP   D   ; 18  discard the RST's return address
0019   E1                     POP   H   ;     new TOS = NOS
001A   C3 31 00               JMP   next0   
001D   E5           H_FROMR:   PUSH   H   ; 1D  "}" return stack to TOS
001E   CF                     RST   1   
001F   F7                     RST   6   
0020                             ; ---- RST 4: neg16: HL = -HL (keeps BC, DE) ----------------------------------
0020   AF           NEG16:    XRA   A   ; 20
0021   95                     SUB   L   
0022   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0023   9F                     SBB   A   
0024   94                     SUB   H   
0025   67                     MOV   H,A   
0026   C9                     RET      
0027   E9           JPHL:     PCHL      ; 27  (for the machine-code call)
0028                             ; ---- RST 5: putc: print A (keeps BC, DE, HL) --------------------------------
0028                RST28:       
0028                          IFN   CPM   
0028   C3 03 FF     PUTC:     JMP   CONOUT   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                          IF   CPM   
                              JMP   putc   ; 28
002B                          ENDIF      
002B                             ; exec: "`" with no hex digit after it: call the machine code at TOS. It
002B                             ; returns here, with its top cell on the stack: that becomes the new TOS.
002B   CD 27 00     EXEC:     CALL   jphl   ; 2B
002E   E1                     POP   H   
002F   F7                     RST   6   
0030                             ; ---- RST 6: next character --------------------------------------------------
0030   D1           RST30:    POP   D   ; 30  discard the RST's return address
0031                          IF   CPM   
                              JMP   next0   ; (this copy runs in page zero)
0031                          ENDIF      
0031                VECEND:      
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                             ;  The inner loop: read one character and sort it by range.
0031                             ; 
0031                             ;    00h          end of program
0031                             ;    01h-20h, 7Fh-FFh   ignored (control, space, DEL, high bytes)
0031                             ;    30h-39h      digit: read a whole number
0031                             ;    41h-5Ah      A-Z: call the word in that letter's cell
0031                             ;    61h-7Ah      a-z: push the address of that letter's cell
0031                             ;    the rest     punctuation: jump through PTAB, 32 entries, in code order
0031                             ; =============================================================================
0031                NEXT0:       
0031                          IF   CHECKED   
0031   CD A6 04               CALL   chkstk   ; both stacks are checked once per character
0034                          ENDIF      
0034   0A                     LDAX   B   
0035   03                     INX   B   
0036   D6 21                  SUI   21h   ; A = c - 21h
0038   DA 7A 00               JC   ctl   ; c < 21h: NUL ends, the rest are ignored
003B   FE 0F                  CPI   0Fh   
003D   DA 6B 00               JC   punct   ; 21h-2Fh: PTAB index 0-14
0040   D6 0F                  SUI   0Fh   ; A = c - 30h
0042   FE 0A                  CPI   0Ah   
0044   DA 5A 02               JC   digit   ; 30h-39h
0047   FE 11                  CPI   11h   
0049   DA 69 00               JC   p3a   ; 3Ah-40h
004C   D6 11                  SUI   11h   ; A = c - 41h
004E   FE 1A                  CPI   1Ah   
0050   DA A9 00               JC   upper   ; 41h-5Ah: A = letter index 0-25
0053   FE 20                  CPI   20h   
0055   DA 67 00               JC   p5b   ; 5Bh-60h
0058   FE 3A                  CPI   3Ah   
005A   DA A3 00               JC   lower   ; 61h-7Ah: A = 20h-39h (cell +64 bytes)
005D   FE 3E                  CPI   3Eh   
005F                          IF   CHECKED   
005F   CA 31 00               JZ   next0   ; 7Fh, DEL: ignored
0062   D2 DD 04               JNC   e_hi   ; 80h-FFh: reserved
0065                          ENDIF      
0065                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              JNC   next0   ; 7Fh-FFh: ignored
0065                          ENDIF      
0065   D6 1A                  SUI   1Ah   ; 7Bh-7Eh: -1Eh in all, index 28-31
0067   D6 09        P5B:      SUI   9   ; 5Bh-60h: -4 in all, index 22-27
0069   C6 05        P3A:      ADI   5   ; 3Ah-40h: index 15-21
006B                             ; Punctuation: A = the PTAB index. The handler starts with HL = TOS,
006B                             ; untouched, and A, DE free.
006B   C6 3A        PUNCT:    ADI   PTAB & 0FFh   ; PTAB never crosses a page
006D   5F                     MOV   E,A   
006E   16 02                  MVI   D,PTAB / 256   
0070   FE 50                  CPI   (PTAB & 0FFh) + NPG1   ; carry: one of the first NPG1
0072   1A                     LDAX   D   
0073   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; the handler's low byte
0074                          IFN   CPM   
0074   3E 00                  MVI   A,0   
0076   17                     RAL      ; its page: 0 + carry
0077                          ENDIF      
0077                          IF   CPM   
                              MVI   A,1   
                              ACI   0   ; its page: 1 + carry
0077                          ENDIF      
0077   57                     MOV   D,A   
0078   D5                     PUSH   D   ; jump to it; the stack is balanced again
0079   C9                     RET      ;   when the handler starts
007A                             ; ctl: characters below 21h. A = c - 21h.
007A   C6 21        CTL:      ADI   21h   ; back to c; zero only for NUL
007C   C2 31 00               JNZ   next0   ; the rest are ignored
007F   C3 09 FF     ENDPROG:   JMP   EXIT   ; the program has ended
0082                             ; =============================================================================
0082                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's first page: ^ _ ` | ~
0082                             ;  (00bbIGFuZCA= are up among the RST routines.)
0082                             ; =============================================================================
0082   D1           H_XOR:    POP   D   
0083   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0084   AA                     XRA   D   
0085   67                     MOV   H,A   
0086   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0087   AB                     XRA   E   
0088   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0089   F7                     RST   6   
008A   D1           H_OR:     POP   D   
008B   7C                     MOV   A,H   
008C   B2                     ORA   D   
008D   67                     MOV   H,A   
008E   7D                     MOV   A,L   
008F   B3                     ORA   E   
0090   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0091   F7                     RST   6   
0092   E7           H_NOT:    RST   4   ; ~x = -x - 1
0093   2B                     DCX   H   
0094   F7                     RST   6   
0095                             ; "_" ( n -- addr ): the heap pointer moves by n, a signed count (the add is
0095                             ; the same either way); TOS is the old pointer.
0095   EB           H_ALLOC:   XCHG      
0096   2A 7C 82               LHLD   HEAP   
0099   E5                     PUSH   H   
009A   19                     DAD   D   ; the new top
009B                          IF   CHECKED   
009B   CD 54 04               CALL   chkhp   
009E                          ENDIF      
009E   22 7C 82               SHLD   HEAP   
00A1   E1                     POP   H   
00A2   F7                     RST   6   
00A3                             ; ---- the letters and digits --------------------------------------------------
00A3                             ; a-z: push the cell's address (the cell is the variable)
00A3   E5           LOWER:    PUSH   H   
00A4   87                     ADD   A   
00A5   6F                     MOV   L,A   
00A6   26 82                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   
00A8   F7                     RST   6   
00A9                             ; A-Z: call the word. The return address (the IP after the letter) goes on
00A9                             ; the return stack, and the IP becomes the address in the letter's cell.
00A9   E5           UPPER:    PUSH   H   ; keep TOS: rpushd pops it back
00AA   87                     ADD   A   
00AB   6F                     MOV   L,A   
00AC   26 82                  MVI   H,LETPAGE   ; HL -> cell
00AE   50                     MOV   D,B   
00AF   59                     MOV   E,C   ; DE = the return address
00B0   4E                     MOV   C,M   
00B1   23                     INX   H   
00B2   46                     MOV   B,M   ; IP = the word's body, and fall into rpushd
00B3                             ; rpushd: push DE on the return stack, then pop TOS off the data stack and
00B3                             ; go on. Every push of the return stack ends here: for a word call the cell
00B3                             ; popped is the TOS that upper parked; for "(" and "{" it is the cell under
00B3                             ; the one that was used up.
00B3                             ; 
00B3                             ; The break key is looked at here, so at every word call and loop-back (and
00B3                             ; block entry and "{"), but only one time in 256: BRKCNT counts them. Reading
00B3                             ; the keyboard can be slow (it is a BDOS call under CP/M).
00B3   2A 34 82     RPUSHD:   LHLD   RSP   
00B6   2B                     DCX   H   
00B7   72                     MOV   M,D   
00B8   2B                     DCX   H   
00B9   73                     MOV   M,E   
00BA   22 34 82               SHLD   RSP   
00BD   21 36 82               LXI   H,BRKCNT   
00C0   35                     DCR   M   
00C1   E1                     POP   H   ; (keeps the flags)
00C2   CC 11 04               CZ   pollk   
00C5   F7                     RST   6   
00C6                             ; ---- the grave -------------------------------------------------------------
00C6                             ; The grave is a prefix: with the character after it, it is one command.
00C6                             ; GTAB holds each character with the place of its handler, as a byte to add
00C6                             ; to gbase. The handler starts with HL = TOS, A = the character and the
00C6                             ; carry clear. A character that is not in the table is unsafe: the unchecked
00C6                             ; build searches on through memory, the checked build stops with W.
00C6   0A           H_GRAVE:   LDAX   B   
00C7   03                     INX   B   
00C8   E5                     PUSH   H   ; TOS
00C9   21 70 03               LXI   H,GTAB-1   
00CC   23           GR1:      INX   H   
00CD                          IF   CHECKED   
00CD   5E                     MOV   E,M   
00CE   1C                     INR   E   
00CF   CA 6D 03               JZ   gbad   ; FFh ends the table
00D2                          ENDIF      
00D2   BE                     CMP   M   
00D3   23                     INX   H   
00D4   C2 CC 00               JNZ   gr1   
00D7   5E                     MOV   E,M   
00D8   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
00DA   21 AF 02               LXI   H,gbase   
00DD   19                     DAD   D   ; the handler
00DE   E3                     XTHL      ; TOS back, and jump there
00DF   C9                     RET      
00E0                             ; ---- where the two pages meet ----------------------------------------------
00E0                             ; The first page ends somewhere among the next four handlers, ] \ [ @ (they
00E0                             ; are in falling code order for this), and where exactly differs between the
00E0                             ; builds: NPG1 follows. Every handler below these four must start in the
00E0                             ; second page, and every one above in the first; chktab.py checks both.
00E0                             ; "]" returns: pop an address and jump to it. TOS is parked on the stack
00E0                             ; while rpop uses HL, and the drop at the end brings it back.
00E0   E5           H_RET:    PUSH   H   
00E1   CF           RET2:     RST   1   
00E2   44                     MOV   B,H   
00E3   4D                     MOV   C,L   
00E4   DF                     RST   3   
00E5                             ; "\" ( flag -- ): true skips to the next ")" or "]" at this level; ")"
00E5                             ; drops the block start, "]" returns. No closer at all ends the program.
00E5                             ; The flag stays in HL as the spent cell that rdrop and ret2 drop.
00E5   7C           H_BREAK:   MOV   A,H   
00E6   B5                     ORA   L   
00E7   CA D2 01               JZ   h_drop   ; false: just drop the flag
00EA   CD A7 03               CALL   skip   
00ED   B7                     ORA   A   ; skip returns 0 for ")"
00EE   C2 E1 00               JNZ   ret2   
00F1   C3 06 00               JMP   rdrop   
00F4                             ; "[" followed by a letter stores the body"s address in that letter"s cell:
00F4                             ; uppercase is a word, lowercase a variable. Followed by a space it pushes
00F4                             ; the body"s address instead. Either way it then skips to the matching "]'.
00F4                             ; (The unchecked build takes anything that is not a letter as the space; the
00F4                             ; checked build stops on it.)
00F4   0A           H_DEF:    LDAX   B   
00F5   03                     INX   B   
00F6   D6 41                  SUI   "A"   ; a letter gives 0-25 or 32-57: lowercase
00F8   5F                     MOV   E,A   ;   lands 64 bytes up
00F9   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   ; fold case
00FB   FE 1A                  CPI   26   
00FD   D2 0D 01               JNC   def2   ; not a letter
0100   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0101   87                     ADD   A   
0102   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0103   16 82                  MVI   D,LETPAGE   ; DE -> cell
0105   79                     MOV   A,C   
0106   12                     STAX   D   
0107   1C                     INR   E   
0108   78                     MOV   A,B   
0109   12                     STAX   D   
010A   C3 16 01               JMP   skipnx   
010D                DEF2:        
010D                          IF   CHECKED   
010D   7B                     MOV   A,E   
010E   FE DF                  CPI   " "-"A"+256   
0110   C2 F7 04               JNZ   e_brack   ; anything but a letter or a space
0113                          ENDIF      
0113   E5                     PUSH   H   ; an anonymous block: push its address
0114   60                     MOV   H,B   
0115   69                     MOV   L,C   
0116                SKIPNX:      
0116                          IF   CHECKED   
0116   0B                     DCX   B   ; back onto the letter, so that skip finds its
0117                          ENDIF      ;   opener, the "[", just before where it starts
0117   CD A7 03     SKIPO:    CALL   skip   
011A   F7                     RST   6   
011B   5E           H_FETCH:   MOV   E,M   ; "@"
011C   23                     INX   H   
011D   56                     MOV   D,M   
011E   EB                     XCHG      
011F   F7                     RST   6   
0120                             ; =============================================================================
0120                             ;  Handlers that must start in the image's second page.
0120                             ;  "?" is the last (with "," inside it in the unchecked build), so its long
0120                             ;  tail may run past that page.
0120                             ; =============================================================================
0120                             ; ---- flow control ----------------------------------------------------------
0120                             ; "(" ( flag -- ): true pushes the block start and enters; false skips to
0120                             ; the matching ")".
0120   7C           H_OPEN:   MOV   A,H   
0121   B5                     ORA   L   
0122   E1                     POP   H   
0123   CA 17 01               JZ   skipo   
0126   E5                     PUSH   H   ; (rpushd pops it again)
0127   50                     MOV   D,B   
0128   59                     MOV   E,C   ; the block starts at the IP
0129   C3 B3 00               JMP   rpushd   
012C                             ; ")" ( flag -- ): true jumps back to the block start (and keeps it); false
012C                             ; drops it and carries on.
012C   7C           H_CLOSE:   MOV   A,H   
012D   B5                     ORA   L   
012E   CA 06 00               JZ   rdrop   
0131   CF                     RST   1   ; pop the block start ...
0132   44                     MOV   B,H   
0133   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; ... jump to it ...
0134   EB                     XCHG      
0135   C3 B3 00               JMP   rpushd   ; ... and push it back (which drops the flag)
0138                             ; ---- arithmetic and logic: ( NOS TOS -- result ) ---------------------------
0138                             ; "-" has two jobs: directly before a digit it starts a negative number.
0138   0A           H_SUB:    LDAX   B   
0139   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
013B   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
013D   DA 60 02               JC   negnum   
0140   E7                     RST   4   ; a - b = a + (-b): fall into "+"
0141   D1           H_ADD:    POP   D   
0142   19                     DAD   D   
0143   F7                     RST   6   
0144   D1           H_AND:    POP   D   
0145   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0146   A2                     ANA   D   
0147   67                     MOV   H,A   
0148   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0149   A3                     ANA   E   
014A   6F                     MOV   L,A   
014B   F7                     RST   6   
014C                             ; Signed compares. Both are "DE < HL" for the right pair: > swaps the two
014C                             ; cells first (XTHL), < doesn't. There is no overflow flag, so the signed
014C                             ; answer is the unsigned borrow of DE - HL, flipped when the signs differ.
014C                             ; SBB A turns a carry into -1 or 0 with no branch.
014C   E3           H_GT:     XTHL      ; a > b  is  b < a
014D   D1           H_LT:     POP   D   ; a < b: DE = a, HL = b
014E   7B                     MOV   A,E   
014F   95                     SUB   L   
0150   7A                     MOV   A,D   
0151   9C                     SBB   H   
0152   9F                     SBB   A   ; A = -1 if DE < HL unsigned
0153   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0154   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0155   AA                     XRA   D   
0156   17                     RAL      ; carry = the signs differ
0157   9F                     SBB   A   
0158   AD                     XRA   L   ; flip when they do
0159   67                     MOV   H,A   
015A   6F                     MOV   L,A   
015B   F7                     RST   6   
015C   D1           H_EQ:     POP   D   
015D   7D                     MOV   A,L   
015E   AB                     XRA   E   
015F   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0160   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0161   AA                     XRA   D   
0162   B5                     ORA   L   ; zero if equal
0163   D6 01                  SUI   1   ; carry only for zero
0165   9F                     SBB   A   
0166   67                     MOV   H,A   
0167   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0168   F7                     RST   6   
0169                             ; "*": shift-and-add on the multiplier's low bit, so it stops as soon as the
0169                             ; multiplier is used up; only the low 16 bits are kept.
0169   D1           H_MUL:    POP   D   ; DE = multiplicand
016A   C5                     PUSH   B   
016B   44                     MOV   B,H   
016C   4D                     MOV   C,L   ; BC = multiplier
016D   21 00 00               LXI   H,0   
0170   78           MUL1:     MOV   A,B   
0171   B7                     ORA   A   ; clear carry
0172   1F                     RAR      
0173   47                     MOV   B,A   
0174   79                     MOV   A,C   
0175   1F                     RAR      
0176   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; BC >> 1, carry = the bit shifted out
0177   D2 7B 01               JNC   mul2   
017A   19                     DAD   D   
017B   EB           MUL2:     XCHG      
017C   29                     DAD   H   ; multiplicand << 1
017D   EB                     XCHG      
017E   78                     MOV   A,B   
017F   B1                     ORA   C   
0180   C2 70 01               JNZ   mul1   
0183   C1                     POP   B   
0184   F7                     RST   6   
0185                             ; "/" ( a b -- q r ): the remainder is on top. Truncates toward zero; r takes
0185                             ; a's sign. Divide |a| by |b|, then q gets the sign of a XOR b and r the sign
0185                             ; of a. Dividing by zero returns two cells of no meaning; the checked build
0185                             ; stops on it.
0185                H_DIV:       
0185                          IF   CHECKED   
0185   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0186   B5                     ORA   L   
0187   CA F4 04               JZ   e_zero   
018A                          ENDIF      
018A   D1                     POP   D   ; DE = a, HL = b
018B   C5                     PUSH   B   
018C   7A                     MOV   A,D   
018D   B7                     ORA   A   
018E   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of a (for r)
018F   AC                     XRA   H   
0190   F5                     PUSH   PSW   ; S flag = sign of q
0191   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0192   B7                     ORA   A   
0193   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; HL = |b|
0196   EB                     XCHG      
0197   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0198   B7                     ORA   A   
0199   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; HL = |a|, DE = |b|
019C   CD 7D 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = q, BC = r
019F   F1                     POP   PSW   
01A0   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; q's sign
01A3   EB                     XCHG      ; DE = q
01A4   60                     MOV   H,B   
01A5   69                     MOV   L,C   ; HL = r
01A6   F1                     POP   PSW   
01A7   FC 20 00               CM   neg16   ; r's sign
01AA   C1                     POP   B   
01AB   D5                     PUSH   D   ; q under r
01AC   F7                     RST   6   
01AD                             ; ---- stack and storage -----------------------------------------------------
01AD   E5           H_DUP:    PUSH   H   ; ":"
01AE   F7                     RST   6   
01AF   E3           H_SWAP:   XTHL      ; "%"
01B0   F7                     RST   6   
01B1                             ; (The checked build tests the address before it takes the value off the
01B1                             ; stack, so that an error report shows both.)
01B1                H_STORE:      ; "!" ( n addr -- )
01B1                          IF   CHECKED   
01B1   CD 6A 04               CALL   chkst   
01B4                          ENDIF      
01B4   D1                     POP   D   
01B5   73                     MOV   M,E   
01B6   23                     INX   H   
01B7   72                     MOV   M,D   
01B8   DF                     RST   3   
01B9                H_CSTORE:      ; "." ( c addr -- )
01B9                          IF   CHECKED   
01B9   CD 6A 04               CALL   chkst   
01BC                          ENDIF      
01BC   D1                     POP   D   
01BD   73                     MOV   M,E   
01BE   DF                     RST   3   
01BF                             ; ---- console ---------------------------------------------------------------
01BF                             ; 22h pushes the address of the text after it and skips the string.
01BF   E5           H_STR:    PUSH   H   
01C0   60                     MOV   H,B   
01C1   69                     MOV   L,C   
01C2   CD EB 03               CALL   skipstr   
01C5                          IF   CHECKED   
01C5   B7                     ORA   A   ; 0: the text ran out before the closing quote
01C6   CA EC 04               JZ   e_quote   
01C9                          ENDIF      
01C9   F7                     RST   6   
01CA                             ; "$" prints the string at TOS, decoding escapes: "/" plus a character
01CA                             ; clears that character"s bit 6 (/M is CR, /` is space; "/" and ""' have no
01CA                             ; bit 6, so // and /" give themselves).
01CA                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    H_PRINT:   MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JZ   h_drop   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JNZ   pr1   
                              MOV   A,M   
                              INX   H   
                              ANI   0BFh   
                    PR1:      RST   5   
                              JMP   h_print   
01CA                          ENDIF      
01CA                          IF   CHECKED   
01CA                             ; (The checked build has the loop as a routine, prstr, which the error
01CA                             ; report uses too. The address is kept on the stack meanwhile: a report
01CA                             ; shows the stack as it was before the "$".)
01CA   E5           H_PRINT:   PUSH   H   
01CB   CD 7D 04               CALL   prstr   
01CE   D1                     POP   D   
01CF   DF                     RST   3   
01D0                          ENDIF      
01D0   7D           H_EMIT:   MOV   A,L   ; "'"
01D1   EF                     RST   5   
01D2   DF           H_DROP:   RST   3   ; ";" is this one byte
01D3                             ; "#" prints TOS as a signed decimal number, with no space after it.
01D3   C5           H_NUM:    PUSH   B   
01D4   CD 8C 03               CALL   psgn   
01D7   C1                     POP   B   
01D8   DF                     RST   3   
01D9                          IF   CHECKED   ; (the checked build has no room to start ","
01D9   6E           H_CFETCH:   MOV   L,M   ;   as late as the unchecked one does: see
01DA   26 00                  MVI   H,0   ;   the end of "?")
01DC   F7                     RST   6   
01DD                          ENDIF      
01DD                             ; "?" ( n -- c ) or ( -n -- addr )
01DD                             ;   n > 0: wait about n ms for a key; 0 if none came
01DD                             ;   n = 0: wait for a key
01DD                             ;   n < 0: read a line of at most -n characters, with echo. The buffer
01DD                             ;          holds 127 characters and the CR: a bigger count is taken as 127.
01DD   7C           H_KEY:    MOV   A,H   
01DE   B7                     ORA   A   
01DF   FA 06 02               JM   line   
01E2   1E 28        KT1:      MVI   E,MSLOOP   ; one millisecond, roughly
01E4   CD 43 04     KT2:      CALL   getk   
01E7   C2 02 02               JNZ   kt3   
01EA   1D                     DCR   E   
01EB   C2 E4 01               JNZ   kt2   
01EE   EB                     XCHG      ; a millisecond with no key stirs the random
01EF   2A 76 82               LHLD   SEED   ;   seed by one: how long a key takes to come
01F2   23                     INX   H   ;   is the one thing here that is not the
01F3   22 76 82               SHLD   SEED   ;   same every time
01F6   EB                     XCHG      
01F7   7C                     MOV   A,H   ; 0? never counts down: it waits
01F8   B5                     ORA   L   
01F9   CA E2 01               JZ   kt1   
01FC   2B                     DCX   H   
01FD   7C                     MOV   A,H   
01FE   B5                     ORA   L   
01FF   C2 E2 01               JNZ   kt1   ; A = 0 if the time ran out
0202                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              DB   0FEh   ; (CPI: steps over the one byte of ",")
                    H_CFETCH:   MOV   A,M   ; "," shares "?"s ending: A becomes TOS
0202                          ENDIF      
0202   6F           KT3:      MOV   L,A   
0203   26 00                  MVI   H,0   
0205   F7                     RST   6   
0206                          IF   CPM   
                                 ; CP/M: BDOS 10 does the editing (the spec allows the platform's
                                 ; own line editor). It doesn't store the CR, so it is added here.
                    LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
                              DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
                              SBB   A   
                              ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
                              XRI   127   ; A = the count, 127 at most
                              STA   LBHDR   
                              PUSH   B   
                              LXI   D,LBHDR   
                              MVI   C,10   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   B   
                              LXI   H,LBHDR+1   
                              MOV   A,M   ; the count typed (0-127)
                              INR   L   ; HL = LINEBUF, whose low byte is 80h:
                              ADD   L   ;   adding the count to L can't carry
                              MOV   L,A   
                              MVI   M,13   
                              MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
                              RST   6   
0206                          ENDIF      
0206                          IFN   CPM   
0206                             ; Generic: Backspace takes the last character back (and is echoed as
0206                             ; it is), CR ends (stored, not echoed), every other key is stored and
0206                             ; echoed until the line is full. The line buffer starts at offset 80h
0206                             ; of its page, so L alone is the place in the line: D holds the L of
0206                             ; a full line.
0206   11 7F 00     LINE:     LXI   D,127   ; TOS is minus the count: adding 127 carries
0209   19                     DAD   D   ;   only for 1 to 127, and leaves 127 - count
020A   9F                     SBB   A   
020B   A5                     ANA   L   ; (0 for a count that is too big)
020C   2F                     CMA      
020D   57                     MOV   D,A   ; D = the L of a full line: 80h + count, FFh
020E                             ;   at most
020E   21 80 82               LXI   H,LINEBUF   
0211   CD 43 04     LN2:      CALL   getk   
0214   CA 11 02               JZ   ln2   
0217   FE 0D                  CPI   13   
0219   CA 36 02               JZ   ln5   
021C   FE 08                  CPI   8   
021E   CA 2E 02               JZ   ln4   
0221   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0222   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0223   BA                     CMP   D   
0224   CA 11 02               JZ   ln2   ; full
0227   73                     MOV   M,E   
0228   2C                     INR   L   
0229   7B                     MOV   A,E   
022A   EF           LN3:      RST   5   
022B   C3 11 02               JMP   ln2   
022E   2D           LN4:      DCR   L   ; Backspace: one back, and echo it,
022F   FA 2A 02               JM   ln3   ;   unless the line was empty (L left the
0232   2C                     INR   L   ;   upper half of the page)
0233   C3 11 02               JMP   ln2   
0236   77           LN5:      MOV   M,A   ; the CR
0237   2E 80                  MVI   L,LINEBUF & 0FFh   
0239   F7                     RST   6   
023A                          ENDIF      
023A                             ; =============================================================================
023A                             ;  Dispatch table: the low byte of each handler's address, in code order.
023A                             ;  It must not cross a page (the dispatcher only adds to its low byte).
023A                             ; =============================================================================
023A                             ; The handlers of the first NPG1 characters start in the image's second page.
023A                             ; ] \ [ @ sit where the two pages meet, and which side each lands on
023A                             ; differs between the builds, so the count is worked out here.
023A                             ; (One division to a line: asm80 only rounds down when it stores a value.)
023A                PGRET:    EQU   (h_ret-BASE)/256   ; 0 = first page, 1 = second
023A                PGBRK:    EQU   (h_break-BASE)/256   
023A                PGDEF:    EQU   (h_def-BASE)/256   
023A                PGFET:    EQU   (h_fetch-BASE)/256   
023A                NPG1:     EQU   21 + PGFET + PGDEF + PGBRK + PGRET   
023A   B1           PTAB:     DB   h_store & 0FFh   ; !
023B   BF                     DB   h_str & 0FFh   ; "
023C   D3                     DB   h_num & 0FFh   ; #
023D   CA                     DB   h_print & 0FFh   ; $
023E   AF                     DB   h_swap & 0FFh   ; %
023F   44                     DB   h_and & 0FFh   ; &
0240   D0                     DB   h_emit & 0FFh   ; '
0241   20                     DB   h_open & 0FFh   ; (
0242   2C                     DB   h_close & 0FFh   ; )
0243   69                     DB   h_mul & 0FFh   ; *
0244   41                     DB   h_add & 0FFh   ; +
0245   D9                     DB   h_cfetch & 0FFh   ; ,
0246   38                     DB   h_sub & 0FFh   ; -
0247   B9                     DB   h_cstore & 0FFh   ; .
0248   85                     DB   h_div & 0FFh   ; /
0249   AD                     DB   h_dup & 0FFh   ; :
024A   D2                     DB   h_drop & 0FFh   ; ;
024B   4D                     DB   h_lt & 0FFh   ; <
024C   5C                     DB   h_eq & 0FFh   ; =
024D   4C                     DB   h_gt & 0FFh   ; >
024E   DD                     DB   h_key & 0FFh   ; ?
024F   1B                     DB   h_fetch & 0FFh   ; @
0250   F4                     DB   h_def & 0FFh   ; [
0251   E5                     DB   h_break & 0FFh   ; \
0252   E0                     DB   h_ret & 0FFh   ; ]
0253   82                     DB   h_xor & 0FFh   ; ^
0254   95                     DB   h_alloc & 0FFh   ; _
0255   C6                     DB   h_grave & 0FFh   ; `
0256   14                     DB   h_tor & 0FFh   ; {
0257   8A                     DB   h_or & 0FFh   ; |
0258   1D                     DB   h_fromr & 0FFh   ; }
0259   92                     DB   h_not & 0FFh   ; ~
025A                PTABEND:      
025A                             ; =============================================================================
025A                             ;  Routines (no handler starts past this point)
025A                             ; =============================================================================
025A                             ; Digits: step back onto the first digit and read the whole number.
025A   E5           DIGIT:    PUSH   H   
025B   0B                     DCX   B   
025C   CD 66 02               CALL   rdnum   
025F   F7                     RST   6   
0260                             ; negnum: "-" directly before a digit: read the number, negate it.
0260   E5           NEGNUM:   PUSH   H   
0261   CD 66 02               CALL   rdnum   
0264   E7                     RST   4   
0265   F7                     RST   6   
0266                             ; rdnum: read decimal digits at IP into HL; IP is left on the first
0266                             ; non-digit. Values wrap at 16 bits, as the spec says.
0266   21 00 00     RDNUM:    LXI   H,0   
0269   0A           RDN1:     LDAX   B   
026A   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
026C   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
026E   D0                     RNC      
026F   03                     INX   B   
0270   54                     MOV   D,H   
0271   5D                     MOV   E,L   
0272   29                     DAD   H   
0273   29                     DAD   H   
0274   19                     DAD   D   
0275   29                     DAD   H   ; HL * 10
0276   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0277   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
0279   19                     DAD   D   
027A   C3 69 02               JMP   rdn1   
027D                             ; udiv: unsigned HL / DE (DE <= 8000h). Returns HL = quotient, BC = remainder.
027D                             ; Uses A, BC; the caller saves the IP. HL holds the dividend and, as its bits
027D                             ; leave at the top, the quotient bits arrive at the bottom. The loop counter
027D                             ; lives on the stack, since A is busy with the shifts.
027D                             ; Dividing by 2 is one shift (the spec wants that fast).
027D   01 00 00     UDIV:     LXI   B,0   
0280   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0281   EE 02                  XRI   2   
0283   B2                     ORA   D   
0284   C2 91 02               JNZ   udv0   
0287   B4                     ORA   H   ; A was 0, and the carry is clear
0288   1F                     RAR      
0289   67                     MOV   H,A   
028A   7D                     MOV   A,L   
028B   1F                     RAR      
028C   6F                     MOV   L,A   ; the quotient
028D   78                     MOV   A,B   
028E   17                     RAL      
028F   4F                     MOV   C,A   ; the remainder: the bit that fell out
0290   C9                     RET      
0291   3E 10        UDV0:     MVI   A,16   
0293   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
0294   29           UDV1:     DAD   H   ; next dividend bit into the carry
0295   79                     MOV   A,C   
0296   17                     RAL      
0297   4F                     MOV   C,A   
0298   78                     MOV   A,B   
0299   17                     RAL      
029A   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC = BC*2 + bit
029B   79                     MOV   A,C   
029C   93                     SUB   E   
029D   78                     MOV   A,B   
029E   9A                     SBB   D   ; carry if BC < DE
029F   DA A7 02               JC   udv2   
02A2   47                     MOV   B,A   ; BC - DE (high byte; A holds it)
02A3   79                     MOV   A,C   
02A4   93                     SUB   E   
02A5   4F                     MOV   C,A   
02A6   2C                     INR   L   ; quotient bit
02A7   F1           UDV2:     POP   PSW   
02A8   3D                     DCR   A   
02A9   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
02AA   C2 94 02               JNZ   udv1   
02AD   F1                     POP   PSW   
02AE   C9                     RET      
02AF                             ; =============================================================================
02AF                             ;  The grave's codes (h_grave is the dispatcher). Each starts with HL = TOS,
02AF                             ;  A = the character and the carry clear.
02AF                             ; 
02AF                             ;    `!  ( addr -- )        call the machine code at addr (exec)
02AF                             ;    `$  ( addr -- addr' )  the hex loader
02AF                             ;    `'  ( -- )             new line: CR LF
02AF                             ;    `+  ( addr -- n )      add 1 to the cell at addr and leave its new value
02AF                             ;    `,  ( n -- r )         a random number from 0 to n-1 (n is 1 to 32767)
02AF                             ;    `-  ( addr -- n )      subtract 1 from the cell at addr, the same way
02AF                             ;    `.  ( -- addr )        the address of the random seed
02AF                             ;    `<  ( a b -- n )       the smaller of the two (signed)
02AF                             ;    `>  ( a b -- n )       the larger
02AF                             ;    `?  ( flag -- )        the cursor off (0) or on
02AF                             ;    `@  ( row col -- )     the cursor to that row and column, both from 0
02AF                             ;    `^  ( -- )             clear the screen and home the cursor
02AF                             ;    `_  ( -- )             clear from the cursor to the end of the line
02AF                             ; =============================================================================
02AF                GBASE:       
02AF   C3 2B 00     G_EXEC:   JMP   exec   ; (exec is up among the RST routines)
02B2                             ; `$: pairs of hex digits are stored from addr until a non-hex character;
02B2                             ; then a RET (C9h) is written and its address is left. An odd last digit is
02B2                             ; consumed and dropped.
02B2   CD FE 03     G_HEX:    CALL   hexc   
02B5   D2 C9 02               JNC   hx2   
02B8   87                     ADD   A   
02B9   87                     ADD   A   
02BA   87                     ADD   A   
02BB   87                     ADD   A   
02BC   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the high digit
02BD   CD FE 03               CALL   hexc   
02C0   D2 C9 02               JNC   hx2   ; odd digit: consumed and dropped
02C3   B2                     ORA   D   
02C4   77                     MOV   M,A   
02C5   23                     INX   H   
02C6   C3 B2 02               JMP   g_hex   
02C9   36 C9        HX2:      MVI   M,0C9h   ; (never range-checked: the spec says so)
02CB   F7                     RST   6   
02CC   3E 0D        G_NL:     MVI   A,13   
02CE   EF                     RST   5   
02CF   3E 0A                  MVI   A,10   
02D1   EF                     RST   5   
02D2   F7                     RST   6   
02D3                             ; `+ and `-: one routine. The character says which.
02D3                G_INC:       
02D3                          IF   CHECKED   
02D3   CD 6A 04               CALL   chkst   ; the address is tested first, as "!" does
02D6   0B                     DCX   B   
02D7   0A                     LDAX   B   ; (the test used A: the character again)
02D8   03                     INX   B   
02D9                          ENDIF      
02D9   FE 2C                  CPI   ","   ; carry for "+"
02DB   5E                     MOV   E,M   
02DC   23                     INX   H   
02DD   56                     MOV   D,M   
02DE   D2 E3 02               JNC   gi1   
02E1   13                     INX   D   
02E2   13                     INX   D   
02E3   1B           GI1:      DCX   D   
02E4   72                     MOV   M,D   
02E5   2B                     DCX   H   
02E6   73                     MOV   M,E   
02E7   EB                     XCHG      ; the new value is TOS
02E8   F7                     RST   6   
02E9                             ; `. pushes the address of the random seed.
02E9   E5           G_SEED:   PUSH   H   
02EA   21 76 82               LXI   H,SEED   
02ED   F7                     RST   6   
02EE                             ; `, ( n -- r ). The seed goes one step on: seed * 261 + 1, which takes
02EE                             ; every 16-bit value in turn. The high bits of such a seed are the good ones
02EE                             ; and the low ones repeat soon, so the high byte is folded into the low
02EE                             ; (XOR) before the remainder of dividing by n is taken.
02EE                             ; n must be 1 to 32767: the checked build stops with Z on anything less
02EE                             ; than 1.
02EE                G_RND:       
02EE                          IF   CHECKED   
02EE   2B                     DCX   H   
02EF   7C                     MOV   A,H   ; n - 1 negative: n is 0 or less
02F0   23                     INX   H   
02F1   B7                     ORA   A   
02F2   FA F4 04               JM   e_zero   
02F5                          ENDIF      
02F5   EB                     XCHG      ; DE = n
02F6   C5                     PUSH   B   
02F7   2A 76 82               LHLD   SEED   
02FA   44                     MOV   B,H   
02FB   4D                     MOV   C,L   
02FC   29                     DAD   H   
02FD   29                     DAD   H   
02FE   09                     DAD   B   ; * 5
02FF   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0300   81                     ADD   C   
0301   67                     MOV   H,A   ; + * 256: * 261
0302   23                     INX   H   
0303   22 76 82               SHLD   SEED   
0306   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0307   AD                     XRA   L   
0308   6F                     MOV   L,A   
0309   CD 7D 02               CALL   udiv   ; BC = the remainder
030C   60                     MOV   H,B   
030D   69                     MOV   L,C   
030E   C1                     POP   B   
030F   F7                     RST   6   
0310                             ; `< and `>: one routine. b < a (signed) is the borrow of b - a, turned
0310                             ; round if the two signs differ: RAR puts the borrow in bit 7, where the two
0310                             ; XRAs meet it. Then the character is read again, 3Ch or 3Eh: RAR leaves
0310                             ; 1Eh or 1Fh under the flag, and adding 61h carries into the flag for 1Fh
0310                             ; only. So the carry ends up saying "keep b" for either character.
0310   D1           G_MIN:    POP   D   ; DE = a, HL = b
0311   7D                     MOV   A,L   
0312   93                     SUB   E   
0313   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0314   9A                     SBB   D   
0315   1F                     RAR      
0316   AC                     XRA   H   
0317   AA                     XRA   D   
0318   17                     RAL      ; carry: b < a
0319   0B                     DCX   B   
031A   0A                     LDAX   B   
031B   03                     INX   B   
031C   1F                     RAR      
031D   C6 61                  ADI   61h   
031F   17                     RAL      
0320   DA 24 03               JC   gm1   
0323   EB                     XCHG      
0324   F7           GM1:      RST   6   
0325                          IF   ANSI   
0325                             ; `^: ESC [ H homes the cursor, and ESC [ J clears from there to the end of
0325                             ; the screen. `_: ESC [ K clears to the end of the line.
0325   CD 66 03     G_CLS:    CALL   csi   
0328   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   
032A   EF                     RST   5   
032B   3E 4A                  MVI   A,"J"   
032D   11                     DB   11h   ; (LXI D: steps over the two bytes of g_eol)
032E   3E 4B        G_EOL:    MVI   A,"K"   
0330   5F                     MOV   E,A   
0331   CD 66 03               CALL   csi   
0334   7B                     MOV   A,E   
0335   EF                     RST   5   
0336   F7                     RST   6   
0337                             ; `? ( flag -- ): ESC [ ? 2 5 l hides the cursor, ESC [ ? 2 5 h shows it.
0337   CD 66 03     G_CUR:    CALL   csi   
033A   3E 3F                  MVI   A,"?"   
033C   EF                     RST   5   
033D   3E 32                  MVI   A,"2"   
033F   EF                     RST   5   
0340   3E 35                  MVI   A,"5"   
0342   EF                     RST   5   
0343   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0344   B5                     ORA   L   
0345   3E 6C                  MVI   A,"l"   
0347   CA 4C 03               JZ   gc1   
034A   3E 68                  MVI   A,"h"   
034C   EF           GC1:      RST   5   
034D   DF                     RST   3   
034E                             ; `@ ( row col -- ): ESC [ row+1 ; col+1 H. (ANSI counts from 1.)
034E   D1           G_AT:     POP   D   ; DE = the row
034F   C5                     PUSH   B   ; (pdec uses BC)
0350   E5                     PUSH   H   ; the column
0351   EB                     XCHG      
0352   CD 66 03               CALL   csi   
0355   23                     INX   H   
0356   CD 95 03               CALL   pdec   
0359   3E 3B                  MVI   A,";"   
035B   EF                     RST   5   
035C   E1                     POP   H   
035D   23                     INX   H   
035E   CD 95 03               CALL   pdec   
0361   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   
0363   EF                     RST   5   
0364   C1                     POP   B   
0365   DF                     RST   3   
0366                             ; csi: print ESC [, which starts every ANSI sequence. Keeps all but A.
0366   3E 1B        CSI:      MVI   A,27   
0368   EF                     RST   5   
0369   3E 5B                  MVI   A,"["   
036B   EF                     RST   5   
036C   C9                     RET      
036D                          ENDIF      
036D                          IF   1-ANSI   
                                 ; With ANSI = 0 the machine's own routines do the work (see the equates).
                    G_CLS:    CALL   CONCLS   
                              RST   6   
                    G_EOL:    CALL   CONEOL   
                              RST   6   
                    G_CUR:    MOV   A,H   
                              ORA   L   
                              CALL   CONCUR   
                              RST   3   
                    G_AT:     POP   D   ; DE = the row, HL = the column
                              CALL   CONAT   
                              RST   3   
036D                          ENDIF      
036D                          IF   CHECKED   
036D   E1           GBAD:     POP   H   ; no such code: W. The place is the character
036E   C3 F7 04               JMP   e_brack   
0371                          ENDIF      
0371                             ; The table: a character, then its handler's distance from gbase.
0371   21 00        GTAB:     DB   "!",g_exec-gbase   
0373   24 03                  DB   "$",g_hex-gbase   
0375   27 1D                  DB   27h,g_nl-gbase   
0377   2B 24                  DB   "+",g_inc-gbase   
0379   2C 3F                  DB   ",",g_rnd-gbase   
037B   2D 24                  DB   "-",g_inc-gbase   
037D   2E 3A                  DB   ".",g_seed-gbase   
037F   3C 61                  DB   "<",g_min-gbase   
0381   3E 61                  DB   ">",g_min-gbase   
0383   3F 88                  DB   "?",g_cur-gbase   
0385   40 9F                  DB   "@",g_at-gbase   
0387   5E 76                  DB   "^",g_cls-gbase   
0389   5F 7F                  DB   "_",g_eol-gbase   
038B                          IF   CHECKED   
038B   FF                     DB   0FFh   ; the end
038C                          ENDIF      
038C                             ; psgn: print HL as a signed number. Uses BC.
038C   7C           PSGN:     MOV   A,H   
038D   B7                     ORA   A   
038E   F2 95 03               JP   pdec   
0391   3E 2D                  MVI   A,"-"   
0393   EF                     RST   5   
0394   E7                     RST   4   
0395                             ; pdec: print HL unsigned, by recursion on HL / 10 (the stack holds digits).
0395                             ; Uses BC.
0395   11 0A 00     PDEC:     LXI   D,10   
0398   CD 7D 02               CALL   udiv   ; HL = HL / 10, C = the last digit
039B   79                     MOV   A,C   
039C   F5                     PUSH   PSW   
039D   7C                     MOV   A,H   
039E   B5                     ORA   L   
039F   C4 95 03               CNZ   pdec   
03A2   F1                     POP   PSW   
03A3   C6 30                  ADI   "0"   
03A5   EF                     RST   5   
03A6   C9                     RET      
03A7                             ; skip: read past text to the closer at this level, and return A = 0 if it
03A7                             ; was ")" and 2 if it was "]". Brackets of both kinds count together;
03A7                             ; strings are stepped over whole. A NUL first ends the program (for "\" with
03A7                             ; no closer; anything else that runs into the NUL had unbalanced brackets
03A7                             ; anyway). D counts the open levels, starting at 1 for the one we are in:
03A7                             ; skip sets it to 0 and falls through the INR that an opener comes back to.
03A7                             ; 
03A7                             ; The checked build also looks at the character the skip was started by,
03A7                             ; which is always the one just before where it starts: "(" must end at ")",
03A7                             ; "[" at "]", and neither may run into the NUL (N); a string with no closing
03A7                             ; quote counts as running into it. "\" takes either closer. The place where
03A7                             ; the skip started is kept on the stack, for the report.
03A7                SKIP:        
03A7                          IF   CHECKED   
03A7   C5                     PUSH   B   
03A8   0B                     DCX   B   
03A9   0A                     LDAX   B   
03AA   03                     INX   B   
03AB   5F                     MOV   E,A   ; E = the opener: ( [ or \
03AC                          ENDIF      
03AC   16 00                  MVI   D,0   
03AE   14           SK3:      INR   D   ; an opener: one deeper
03AF   0A           SK1:      LDAX   B   
03B0                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              INX   B   
                              ORA   A   
                              JZ   endprog   
03B0                          ENDIF      
03B0                          IF   CHECKED   
03B0   B7                     ORA   A   
03B1   CA DF 03               JZ   sk6   ; (the IP stays on the NUL)
03B4   03                     INX   B   
03B5                          ENDIF      
03B5   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
03B7   CC EB 03               CZ   skipstr   ; leaves A = 22h, which matches nothing below
03BA   D6 28                  SUI   "("   ;   (or 0, and then the NUL is read next)
03BC   CA AE 03               JZ   sk3   
03BF   3D                     DCR   A   ; ")"
03C0   CA CD 03               JZ   sk4   
03C3   D6 32                  SUI   "["-")"   
03C5   CA AE 03               JZ   sk3   
03C8   FE 02                  CPI   "]"-"["   
03CA   C2 AF 03               JNZ   sk1   
03CD   15           SK4:      DCR   D   
03CE                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                              RZ      ; the closer at this level
                              JMP   sk1   
03CE                          ENDIF      
03CE                          IF   CHECKED   
03CE   C2 AF 03               JNZ   sk1   
03D1   57                     MOV   D,A   ; the closer at this level: 0 or 2. Bit 1 of the
03D2   AB                     XRA   E   ;   opener is 0 for "(" and 1 for "[", and only
03D3   E6 06                  ANI   6   ;   "\" has bit 2: so this is 2 for the wrong
03D5   FE 02                  CPI   2   ;   closer, and only then
03D7   7A                     MOV   A,D   
03D8   D1                     POP   D   ; (where the skip started)
03D9   C0                     RNZ      
03DA   42                     MOV   B,D   ; N. The place is the opener
03DB   4B                     MOV   C,E   
03DC   C3 E6 03               JMP   sk7   
03DF   7B           SK6:      MOV   A,E   ; the text ran out:
03E0   E6 04                  ANI   4   
03E2   C2 7F 00               JNZ   endprog   ;   "\" with no closer ends the program
03E5   C1                     POP   B   
03E6   3E 4E        SK7:      MVI   A,"N"   
03E8   C3 FA 04               JMP   errp   ; (errp drops skip's return address)
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                             ; skipstr: IP is inside a string; step past its closing quote. "/" escapes
03EB                             ; the next character, so "/"" does not end it. Leaves A = 22h.
03EB                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    SS0:      INX   B   
                    SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
                              INX   B   
                              CPI   "/"   
                              JZ   ss0   
                              CPI   22h   
                              JNZ   skipstr   
                              RET      
03EB                          ENDIF      
03EB                          IF   CHECKED   
03EB                             ; The checked build never steps over a NUL: if the text runs out first it
03EB                             ; returns A = 0 with the IP on the NUL.
03EB   0A           SKIPSTR:   LDAX   B   
03EC   B7                     ORA   A   
03ED   C8                     RZ      
03EE   03                     INX   B   
03EF   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
03F1   C8                     RZ      
03F2   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
03F4   C2 EB 03               JNZ   skipstr   
03F7   0A                     LDAX   B   ; the escaped character
03F8   B7                     ORA   A   
03F9   C8                     RZ      
03FA   03                     INX   B   
03FB   C3 EB 03               JMP   skipstr   
03FE                          ENDIF      
03FE                             ; hexc: if the character at IP is a hex digit (0-9, A-F, a-f), step over it
03FE                             ; and return its value in A with the carry set; otherwise leave the IP and
03FE                             ; return with the carry clear.
03FE   0A           HEXC:     LDAX   B   
03FF   D6 30                  SUI   "0"   
0401   FE 0A                  CPI   10   
0403   DA 0F 04               JC   hc1   
0406   E6 DF                  ANI   0DFh   
0408   D6 11                  SUI   11h   
040A   FE 06                  CPI   6   
040C   D0                     RNC      
040D   D6 F6                  SUI   0F6h   ; + 10, and sets the carry
040F   03           HC1:      INX   B   
0410   C9                     RET      
0411                             ; =============================================================================
0411                             ;  Console layer. rawk is the host's key routine: a waiting key in A (zero
0411                             ;  flag clear), or A = 0 with the zero flag set when none is waiting. putc
0411                             ;  (RST 5) prints A. Both keep BC, DE and HL. In the generic build they are
0411                             ;  the host's KEY and CONOUT routines themselves.
0411                             ; 
0411                             ;  A running program reads the keyboard only through getk and pollk, which
0411                             ;  between them give the break key its rules:
0411                             ;    - Ctrl-C stops the program;
0411                             ;    - any other key that the break check reads is held in KEYBUF for the
0411                             ;      next "?", and a newer one takes its place;
0411                             ;    - "?" (getk) takes the held key first;
0411                             ;    - a program that has stored a non-zero byte at BRKOFF gets Ctrl-C as a
0411                             ;      key like any other, but two of them within about 250 ms still stop it.
0411                             ;  Both are called straight from a handler, never from a routine under one:
0411                             ;  the checked build's report counts on finding one return address above the
0411                             ;  data stack, and TOS in HL.
0411                             ; =============================================================================
0411                          IFN   CPM   
0411                RAWK:     EQU   KEY   
0411                          ENDIF      
0411                             ; pollk: the break check (see rpushd).
0411   CD 06 FF     POLLK:    CALL   rawk   
0414   C8                     RZ      ; no key
0415   32 7A 82               STA   KEYBUF   ; held for the next "?"
0418   FE 03        PK1:      CPI   3   ; (getk joins here)
041A   C0                     RNZ      
041B                             ; ctlc: Ctrl-C has been read. If the break key is on, that is the end. If
041B                             ; the program has turned it off, wait about 250 ms for one more key: a
041B                             ; second Ctrl-C is the end too; any other key is held (the newest wins),
041B                             ; and the Ctrl-C goes to the program: returns A = 3, zero flag clear.
041B   3A 7B 82     CTLC:     LDA   BRKOFF   
041E   B7                     ORA   A   
041F   CA 78 04               JZ   brk   
0422   D5                     PUSH   D   
0423   11 10 27               LXI   D,250*MSLOOP   
0426   CD 06 FF     CT1:      CALL   rawk   
0429   C2 32 04               JNZ   ct2   
042C   1B                     DCX   D   
042D   7A                     MOV   A,D   
042E   B3                     ORA   E   
042F   C2 26 04               JNZ   ct1   
0432   D1           CT2:      POP   D   ; A = the second key, or 0 if none came
0433   FE 03                  CPI   3   
0435   CA 78 04               JZ   brk   
0438   B7                     ORA   A   
0439   CA 3F 04               JZ   ct3   
043C   32 7A 82               STA   KEYBUF   
043F   3E 03        CT3:      MVI   A,3   
0441   B7                     ORA   A   
0442   C9                     RET      
0443                             ; getk: a key for "?", or A = 0 and the zero flag if there is none.
0443   E5           GETK:     PUSH   H   ; a held key goes first, and is taken out of
0444   21 7A 82               LXI   H,KEYBUF   ;   the buffer
0447   7E                     MOV   A,M   
0448   36 00                  MVI   M,0   
044A   E1                     POP   H   
044B   B7                     ORA   A   
044C   C0                     RNZ      
044D   CD 06 FF               CALL   rawk   
0450   C8                     RZ      
0451   C3 18 04               JMP   pk1   ; Ctrl-C? If not, that is the key
0454                          IF   1-CHECKED   
                    BRK:      EQU   endprog   ; the unchecked build stops without a word;
0454                          ENDIF      
0454                          IF   CHECKED   
0454                BRK:      EQU   e_break   ;   the checked build reports B
0454                          ENDIF      
0454                          IF   CPM   
                    RAWK:     MVI   A,0FFh   ; BDOS 6 with E = FFh: a key, or 0
                                 ; putc: BDOS 6 for every character. BDOS 2 would check for ^S while
                                 ; printing and could swallow a key that BDOS 6 then never sees.
                    PUTC:     PUSH   B   
                              PUSH   D   
                              PUSH   H   
                              MOV   E,A   
                              MVI   C,6   
                              CALL   BDOS   
                              POP   H   
                              POP   D   
                              POP   B   
                              ORA   A   ; (for getk)
                              RET      
0454                          ENDIF      
0454                             ; =============================================================================
0454                             ;  Checked build: the checks and the error report
0454                             ; =============================================================================
0454                          IF   CHECKED   
0454                             ; chkhp: HL = the new heap top, DE = the count, the carry is from adding
0454                             ; it, and the old top is on the stack under the return address. Stop if the
0454                             ; new top is not below the limit page, or is below the program's end.
0454                CHKHP:       
0454                          ENDIF      
0454                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                                 ; With this much room a top that wrapped round can land back in
                                 ; range, so the add is tested too: growing must not carry, and
                                 ; releasing must.
                              MOV   A,D   
                              RAR      ; the carry comes in above the count's sign:
                              ADI   40h   ;   bit 7 = carry XOR sign
                              ADD   A   
                              JC   e_heap   
                              LDA   0007h   
                              DCR   A   
                              CMP   H   
                              JC   e_heap   
0454                          ENDIF      
0454                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
0454                             ; (Here the program's space is under 32K, so a top that wrapped
0454                             ; round always falls outside it.)
0454   7C                     MOV   A,H   
0455   FE F0                  CPI   HEAPLIM   
0457   D2 63 04               JNC   e_heap   
045A                          ENDIF      
045A                          IF   CHECKED   
045A   EB                     XCHG      
045B   E5                     PUSH   H   ; the count
045C   2A 38 82               LHLD   NPEND   
045F   19                     DAD   D   ; carry: at or above the program's end
0460   E1                     POP   H   
0461   EB                     XCHG      
0462   D8                     RC      
0463   EB           E_HEAP:   XCHG      ; put the count back in TOS for the report,
0464   D1                     POP   D   ;   and drop the return address (errp drops
0465   3E 48                  MVI   A,"H"   ;   the old top)
0467   C3 FA 04               JMP   errp   
046A                             ; chkst: stop unless HL is in the program's own space: from the letter page
046A                             ; up to the heap limit (the OS, or HEAPLIM), so the interpreter's stacks and
046A                             ; whatever lies above the limit are safe. Memory above the heap top but
046A                             ; below the limit is the program's own: Tiny BASIC keeps its lines there.
046A                             ; It is the page of HL + 1 that is tested, so that one test serves both
046A                             ; bytes of a cell: the last byte below the limit can"t be stored to with ".'.
046A                             ; Keeps HL and BC. It runs on into its own error entry.
046A   23           CHKST:    INX   H   
046B   7C                     MOV   A,H   
046C   2B                     DCX   H   
046D   FE 82                  CPI   LETPAGE   
046F   DA 75 04               JC   e_store   
0472                          ENDIF      
0472                          IF   CHECKED*(1-CPM)   
0472   FE F0                  CPI   HEAPLIM   
0474   D8                     RC      
0475                          ENDIF      
0475                          IF   CHECKED*CPM   
                              MOV   E,A   
                              LDA   0007h   ; the BDOS page is the heap limit
                              DCR   A   
                              CMP   E   
                              RNC      
0475                          ENDIF      
0475                          IF   CHECKED   
0475                             ; Two error entries for errors found inside a routine: the first hides the
0475                             ; second inside a 3-byte LXI D (the 11h); errp then drops the routine's
0475                             ; return address.
0475   3E 4F        E_STORE:   MVI   A,"O"   ; a store outside the program's space
0477   11                     DB   11h   
0478   3E 42        E_BREAK:   MVI   A,"B"   ; Ctrl-C (found inside pollk or getk)
047A   C3 FA 04               JMP   errp   
047D                             ; prstr: print the string at HL, to its closing quote, decoding "/" (this is
047D                             ; "$", and the error report's texts). A NUL first is an error: Q.
047D   7E           PRSTR:    MOV   A,M   
047E   23                     INX   H   
047F   FE 22                  CPI   22h   
0481   C8                     RZ      
0482   B7                     ORA   A   
0483   CA 93 04               JZ   e_dollar   
0486   FE 2F                  CPI   "/"   
0488   C2 8F 04               JNZ   prs1   
048B   7E                     MOV   A,M   
048C   23                     INX   H   
048D   E6 BF                  ANI   0BFh   
048F   EF           PRS1:     RST   5   
0490   C3 7D 04               JMP   prstr   
0493   D1           E_DOLLAR:   POP   D   ; "$" ran into a NUL: drop the return address,
0494   E1                     POP   H   ;   and put the string's address back in TOS
0495   3E 51                  MVI   A,"Q"   
0497   C3 FB 04               JMP   error   
049A                             ; pmsg: print the text that follows the CALL, to its closing quote. Keeps HL.
049A                             ; pnl: the same, on a new line.
049A   3E 0D        PNL:      MVI   A,13   
049C   EF                     RST   5   
049D   3E 0A                  MVI   A,10   
049F   EF                     RST   5   
04A0   E3           PMSG:     XTHL      
04A1   CD 7D 04               CALL   prstr   
04A4   E3                     XTHL      
04A5   C9                     RET      
04A6                             ; chkstk: both stacks are checked once per character, not in every handler.
04A6                             ; The data stack is right when SP lies in the 256 bytes below DSTOP: adding
04A6                             ; the constant carries if it is above (cells were popped that were never
04A6                             ; pushed), and leaves a high byte of FFh if it is in range. Errors are found
04A6                             ; a character late at most: the bytes above DSTOP and the guard band below
04A6                             ; the page take what happens meanwhile.
04A6   EB           CHKSTK:   XCHG      ; DE = TOS (HL is needed for the pointers)
04A7   21 05 7E               LXI   H,(1-DSTOP)&0FFFFh   ; (SP is 2 lower here: the call)
04AA   39                     DAD   SP   
04AB   DA D5 04               JC   e_under   
04AE   24                     INR   H   
04AF   C2 CF 04               JNZ   e_over   
04B2   2A 34 82               LHLD   RSP   ; the return stack: in its page (or it has
04B5   7C                     MOV   A,H   ;   overflowed), and not above its empty
04B6   FE 80                  CPI   RSPAGE   ;   position (an underflow stays inside the
04B8   C2 CC 04               JNZ   e_rover   ;   page, in the guard band)
04BB   7D                     MOV   A,L   
04BC   FE E1                  CPI   RSTOP&0FFh+1   
04BE   D2 C3 04               JNC   e_runder   
04C1   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
04C2   C9                     RET      
04C3   21 E0 80     E_RUNDER:   LXI   H,RSTOP   ; return stack underflow: it counts as empty
04C6   22 34 82               SHLD   RSP   
04C9   3E 72                  MVI   A,"r"   
04CB   21                     DB   21h   ; (LXI H hides the next entry; HL is free)
04CC   3E 52        E_ROVER:   MVI   A,"R"   ; return stack overflow
04CE   21                     DB   21h   
04CF   3E 53        E_OVER:   MVI   A,"S"   ; data stack overflow
04D1   EB                     XCHG      ; TOS back
04D2   C3 FA 04               JMP   errp   
04D5   31 FC 81     E_UNDER:   LXI   SP,DSTOP   ; data stack underflow: it counts as empty
04D8   3E 73                  MVI   A,"s"   
04DA   C3 FB 04               JMP   error   
04DD                             ; e_hi: the inner loop read a reserved byte, 80h-FFh: X. But a word cell that
04DD                             ; was never defined still holds 0000h, and the byte there is a JMP, C3h, in
04DD                             ; every build: if the IP is in page zero, this was a call of an undefined
04DD                             ; word. The call is undone, so the place is the call itself.
04DD   04           E_HI:     INR   B   
04DE   05                     DCR   B   
04DF   C2 F1 04               JNZ   e_resv   
